<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Raw NASA light curves, not the Kaggle set</p>
    <h1>Finding real planets in raw telescope data</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      A from-scratch transit-detection pipeline: pull raw photometry from NASA's public archive, detrend it,
      run the same classical search astronomers use, and check the answers against known planets before
      pointing it at real, unconfirmed candidates.
    </p>

    <figure class="hero-figure">
      <img
        src="/images/trappist1b_sync_animation.gif"
        alt="A simulated planet crossing a simulated star, synced to the real dip in TRAPPIST-1's light curve"
        width="1160"
        height="480"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Figure 1. TRAPPIST-1 b: a simulated transit, physically sized to the real ~0.7% depth, synced to the
        actual, detrended K2 light curve, phase-folded at the period this pipeline recovered on its own.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</header>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 80px 0 0;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.4vw, 3.1rem);
    max-width: 15ch;
    margin-bottom: 0.3em;
  }
  .dek {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .hero-figure img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
